xnu 0361: watch a catalog record go from having blocks to having none

Three files reach `hfs_getnewvnode` with a size and zero blocks -- `prng.seed`
(32 bytes), `launchd_cache_loader.log` (375) and
`com.apple.mobileassetd-MobileAssetBrain` (6905) -- and every lookup of them marks
the volume inconsistent and fails with EINVAL. `tools/hfs-audit.py` finds no such
record in the image, so the disagreement is created during the boot or the lookup
reads it wrong, and those are different bugs.

Two prints, both only on that shape: the record as `cat_lookupbykey` reads it,
and the fork as `catrec_update` writes it, with the values it replaces. The pair
says whether the record is already broken on disk when it is first looked at, or
whether a writer put it there.

diff --git a/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/hfs_catalog.c b/bsd/mondrian_hfs/core/hfs_catalog.c
